# Accessibility

Target WCAG 2.2 AA. Automated checks do not replace manual keyboard, zoom, contrast, and screen-reader notes.

- Light background, high-contrast text, generous spacing. Small text is the default, about 16px. Normal is about 18px and Larger is about 22px. A journey is a timeline with the line name and color together.
- Touch targets at least 48×48 CSS pixels, with visible text labels. Placeholders do not replace labels.
- Line color is always paired with the line name. Do not use color as the only distinction.
- Keep keyboard focus visible and in a sensible order. Announce route results and form errors.
- Support browser zoom and a visible larger-text control. At 200% text, controls stay usable.
- At narrow widths, the page does not scroll sideways. The map may pan inside its own region.
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`. No essential swipe, hover, long-press, or pinch-only action.
- The interface is English only. Do not add Hindi chrome, theme names, or a language control.
